        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 10th November 1996 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed, confirming hyperinflation and mild hypoxaemia without significant hypercapnia. Spirometry supported severe obstructive ventilatory impairment consistent with his known diagnosis. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a short course of systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded well to treatment with notable symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 11th November 1996 in stable condition. Please ensure continuation of his inhaler regimen and close outpatient follow-up. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
